# Cursor Rules for Skillment Project

## Project Structure
- Monorepo using pnpm workspaces
- Apps in /apps directory
- Shared packages in /packages directory
- Each app has its own package.json and configuration

## Code Organization
- Components in /components directory
- Hooks in /hooks directory
- Utils in /lib directory
- API routes in /app/api directory
- Styles in /styles directory

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., OrgLoginModal)
- Files: kebab-case (e.g., org-login-modal.tsx)
- Functions: camelCase
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- Types/Interfaces: PascalCase with 'I' prefix for interfaces

## Component Patterns
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Props interface defined at top of file
- Destructure props in function parameters
- Use React hooks for state management
- Implement error boundaries for error handling

## Styling Patterns
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Custom components extend shadcn/ui
- Dark theme by default
- Responsive design using Tailwind breakpoints
- Custom animations using Framer Motion

## State Management
- Local state with useState
- Global state with Context API
- Custom hooks for shared logic
- Form state with React Hook Form
- API state with React Query

## API Patterns
- RESTful endpoints
- JWT authentication
- Error handling middleware
- Request validation
- Rate limiting

## Testing Strategy
- Unit tests for components
- Integration tests for features
- E2E tests for critical flows
- API tests for endpoints
- Use Jest and React Testing Library

## Documentation
- JSDoc comments for functions
- README files in each directory
- TypeScript types for all props
- API documentation with OpenAPI
- Component documentation with Storybook

## Git Workflow
- Feature branches from main
- Pull request reviews required
- Conventional commits
- Semantic versioning
- Automated CI/CD

## Performance Guidelines
- Code splitting with Next.js
- Image optimization
- Lazy loading components
- Memoization where needed
- Bundle size monitoring

## Security Practices
- Environment variables for secrets
- Input validation
- XSS prevention
- CSRF protection
- Rate limiting

## Accessibility
- Semantic HTML
- ARIA attributes
- Keyboard navigation
- Screen reader support
- Color contrast compliance 